# What a graph draws: every node's touches and what it does instead, each drawn by its own method where it is.
# `flat_map` hands its closure each node of the graph, and the closure calls `drawn` on each touch of the node and each
# of what it does instead (`chain` goes on with the elements it is handed). The closure's `t` is an element of the node,
# as `for t in ..` binds it, so `t.drawn()` is `Touch::drawn`, as `.map(Touch::drawn)` and `.map(|t| Touch::drawn(t))`
# are (#170). Every element is a part of the graph the route is handed, glued into the step as a projection is, so the
# step takes the graph and no Touch comes from beyond: the plan is the each pair's (`../rust/clean.plan`).

route drawing.drawn
step drawn/Touch.drawn
step drawn/Touch.drawn/Where()

line entry > drawn call
line Graph·g > drawn value                                    # `g.nodes.iter()`: no step
line Graph·g > drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() value               # `self.op` of each touch, a part of the graph
line drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() > Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() value
line Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() > drawn/Touch.drawn value
line drawn/Touch.drawn > Where@drawn/Touch.drawn value
line Where@drawn/Touch.drawn > drawn value                    # collected and given back
line drawn > Where@drawn value                                # and given, at the route's moment

home Graph·g drawn
home Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() drawn/Touch.drawn
home Where@drawn/Touch.drawn drawn
home Where@drawn drawn

side entry left
